  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 204 AM CDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nMid-level high pressure continues to dominate the weather pattern \nover the forecast period, with warm and mostly rain-free conditions \nexpected. Seabreeze convection will be possible in the afternoons, \nwith the best chances Saturday and Sunday as deep moisture (PWAT \nvalues ~2.1\" along the coast) interacts with an area of vorticity \nriding around the periphery of the ridge. \n\nTemperatures will remain hot, with highs in the 90s along the coast \nto around 105 over the Brush Country. With the increased moisture, \nthough spotty in coverage, more cloud cover is expected this \nweekend, keeping the heat index generally below 110. However, \nisolated locations could see heat index values up to 112 due to lack \nof cloud coverage. By early next week, expect heat advisory \nconditions to return. Additionally, an extreme (4/4) heat risk is in \nplay for the Brush Country starting midweek.",
